      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "**Quick Start Guide for GridDeploy**\n\n**Prerequisites**\n\nBefore you begin, ensure you have the following:\n\n* Docker is running on your machine. You can start it by running `docker start` in your terminal.\n* You have AWS credentials configured in `~/.aws/credentials`. This is required for GridDeploy to authenticate with AWS and deploy your application.\n* You have a `grid.yaml` file in the root of your project. This file is used to configure your deployment settings.\n\n**Step 1: Create a GridDeploy Config**\n\nTo create a `grid.yaml` file, run the following command:\n```bash\ngd create-config --env <env> --config <path>\n```\nReplace `<env>` with the environment you want to deploy to (e.g. `dev`, `stg`, `prod`). Replace `<path>` with the path to your `grid.yaml` file.\n\nThe `grid.yaml` file should contain the following configuration:\n```yaml\n# grid.yaml\n\n# Environment settings\nenv: <env>\n\n# AWS settings\naws_access_key_id: <access_key_id>\naws_secret_access_key: <secret_access_key>\naws_region: <aws_region>\n\n# Docker settings\ndocker_image: <",
